  "id": "semantic-dementia",
  "term": "semantic dementia",
  "definition": "Semantic dementia is a form of frontotemporal dementia in which loss of semantic memory leads to a gradually worsening language problem, and it is linked to marked shrinkage in the temporal lobe. Along with verbal difficulties, it can involve notable social-emotional and behavioral changes.",
